This is a known breaking change. In .NET 10, MAUI adopts Android's **edge-to-edge** display by default, which makes `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` (and its MAUI wrapper `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize`) no longer function.

## Solutions (pick one)

### 1. Use `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (simplest)

MAUI has a built-in scroll manager enabled by default. If it's not working, make sure your input is inside a `ScrollView` or that you haven't disabled it:

```csharp
// In MauiProgram.cs — this is ON by default, but verify you haven't turned it off:
builder.ConfigureMauiHandlers(handlers =>
{
    Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect = false;
});
```

### 2. Handle window insets manually (most reliable for chat UIs)

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.Compatibility;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetListener());
}

private class InsetListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        // Apply bottom padding = max of keyboard or nav bar
        int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);
        v.SetPadding(v.PaddingLeft, v.PaddingTop, v.PaddingRight, bottomPadding);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

### 3. Opt out of edge-to-edge (quick escape hatch)

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);
    // Restore legacy behavior
    Window!.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(true);
}
```

> ⚠️ Option 3 reverses the new default and may be removed in future Android versions.

**Recommendation:** For a chat screen, **option 2** gives you the most control — your bottom input bar will shift up exactly by the keyboard height.
